    "text color" : "[0.75, 0.68, 0.67, 0.902]",
    "content" : "Because no single parameter fully de nes cell viability in all systems, it is o en useful to use multiple approaches to study cytotoxicity. In addition to the HCS DNA Damage Kit, we o er the HCS LIVE⁄DEAD® Green Kit (H10290) and the HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit (H10295), both of which employ the Image-iT® DEAD™ Green viability stain. Additionally, the HCS LIVE/DEAD® Kit provides a choice of two nucleic acid stains—the far-red– uorescent HCS NuclearMask™ Deep Red stain (H10294, Section 12.5) and the blue- uorescent Hoechst 33342 (H1399, H3570, H21492; Section 12.5)—for use as cell-permeant nuclear segmentation tools.  e HCS Mitochondrial Health Kit provides Image-iT® DEAD Green viability stain and Hoechst 33342 stain,"
  }, {
